# Line ending normalization
#
# Go sources are stored normalized as LF in the repository (git's `text`
# conversion) and checked out as CRLF (`eol=crlf`) to match the primary
# Windows development environment. `text` keeps diffs line-ending agnostic
# for cross-platform contributors; `eol=crlf` fixes the worktree form so no
# contributor can accidentally introduce mixed line endings.
#
# Note: this repository deliberately does NOT use `* text=auto`; a top-level
# `* -text` rule keeps all files byte-identical to their committed form
# (immune to the user's global `core.autocrlf`), and the more specific
# `*.go` rule below re-enables line-ending conversion for Go sources only.
* -text
*.go text eol=crlf
